WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.340
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.490
It’s a hot day with
clear skies over Kuchiba City.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.000
On days like these...

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.380
Awesome!

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.750
It just keeps on shaving!

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.840
Electronic shaved ice machines
are amazing!

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.900
I’ll have a large portion!

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.640
Then I’ll have an <i>extra</i> large!

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.890
Is it really <i>that</i> exciting?

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:42.500
Of course it is!

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.400
Just <i>look</i> at this powdery, fluffy ice!

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.380
Huh? It stopped?

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.630
I wonder why.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.130
It worked!

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.030
But then it stopped again.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.540
Hey, look at that, Go!

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.840
The lights are acting up?

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.540
Could it be Gänger playing tricks?

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.340
It might just be a blackout.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.620
So this is where you were!

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.800
Director Sakuragi!
What’s with the electricity?

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.760
Listen up! We detected
strong biological energy!

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.560
This is proof that a rare Pokémon
has appeared!

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.660
A rare Pokémon?!

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.100
Isn’t that...?

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.640
A massive thundercloud...

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.680
Strong biological energy...

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.160
A rare Pokémon...

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:43.620
I got it!

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.360
Thunder is coming!

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.540
Huh?!

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:24.800
A Legendary Raid Battle!!
VS Thunder!

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:31.240
Thunder! Electric Pokémon!
Electric/Flying type!

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:37.440
A legendary Pokémon that is said to live in thunderclouds!
It freely controls lightning bolts!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.610
Director Sakuragi!

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.360
We’re in position!
Thunder hasn’t shown up yet, though.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.800
I see.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.830
But the data indicates a high probability
that it will emerge at the port.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.730
Can you stay there
and keep investigating?

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.550
Be careful, though!

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.310
Of course!

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.970
Awesome! So Thunder’s in there?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.710
I can’t wait to meet it!

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:05.220
If I’m going to catch it, we’ll end up
in an aerial battle, for sure.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.990
So my only choice
is this one... Flygon!

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:09.580
I get it!

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:13.350
But I’ll be the first to battle Thunder!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.130
W-What are you saying?!

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.320
I’ll battle and catch it!

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.400
I will!

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.590
No, me!

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.350
Me!

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.660
Not a chance! It’ll be me!

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.400
Me!

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.040
Huh? The thunderclouds...

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.000
What?!

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.520
Thunder?! Where’s Thunder?

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.870
We didn’t get to see Thunder...

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:51.120
That cloud was so huge,
I was sure Thunder would be in there...

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.100
Thunder, you know?

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.270
Thunder?

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:05.530
Satoshi. Have you ever heard the question
of whether the Egg or the Pokémon came first?

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:13.080
Simply put, whether Pokémon Eggs
or Pokémon themselves appeared in this world first.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.920
Sure...

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:24.630
Continuing with that line of thought,
the Index mentioned Thunder living in thunderclouds.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:31.680
Does it really <i>live</i> in thunderclouds,
or do the thunderclouds form around it?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.810
Um, all right.
I get what you’re saying!

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:39.310
Pokémon are still
wrapped up in mystery.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.650
Nobody’s come up with a clear answer.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.800
Koharu!

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:45.530
You’re taking the bus home today?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.780
Yup.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.950
Dad said he’d probably be late
because the blackout caused a lot of trouble.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.400
I see.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:55.570
Seems the institute is okay
because they have backup power,

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:59.570
but that everything in the refrigerator
has gotten warm.

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:01.290
But this is weird though.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:05.410
Mom told me the power’s
been running just fine at home.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:05.970
Huh?!

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.930
So the blackout’s only right here?!

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.390
Seems like it.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.980
It’s kinda cool, huh?

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.280
Like taking a deep breath.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.240
Like, inhale! Then exhale!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.670
What if...?

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:30.360
Good news, you two!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.740
Thunderclouds have started forming
near the port again!

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:37.110
So Thunder might be in them?

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:39.780
That’s right!
Can you go investigate?

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:41.030
Of course!

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:42.400
C’mon, Go!

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.250
Go?

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:47.720
We go <i>this</i> way!

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:50.680
But the port’s over there!

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:54.970
I came up with an answer
to the “Egg or Pokémon” question!

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.600
...I think.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.740
Well, I mean, probably... Maybe...

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.800
It’s just my gut feeling, but...

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:06.280
In any case,
this is the way we should go!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:12.200
Not “my analysis”,
but “my gut feeling”?

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.110
I feel like he’s becoming
more and more like Satoshi.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.550
Where are we?

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:25.240
The Unmanned Power Plant,
which supplies Sakuragi Institute with electricity.

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:26.550
I see.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:31.430
There’s no thunderclouds,
but you think Thunder is here?

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:35.580
Didn’t I tell you?
I think the Pokémon came first.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:39.500
Even if there’s no thundercloud,
I reckon Thunder is in here!

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:46.690
Come out, Thunder!

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.230
Team Rocket?!

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.570
Brat boy?!

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.450
<i>What are you doing here?!</i>

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:58.200
That’s <i>our</i> line!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.080
No, ours!

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.250
Were you guys responsible
for the blackout?!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.730
What are you talking about?

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:07.750
We’re innocent!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:08.950
Yeah, meow!

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:14.590
We were just here to scout out the place
as a potential second Team Rocket base, meow!

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.030
So you’re doing bad stuff
either way!

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:18.350
You got a problem with that?!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:20.900
Was that...?!

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.230
Thunder!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.560
Thunder?!

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.070
The Legendary Pokémon, Thunder?!

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.530
F-F-F-For real?!

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:34.450
For real?!

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.460
<i>There it is!</i>

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.250
Pocket Monsters!

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:03.480
Thunder

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.290
It’s Thunder!

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.480
It really was here!

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.980
Oh my gosh! Oh my gosh!
It’s a real live Legendary Pokémon!

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.610
So cool!

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:22.380
Electricity’s gathering around Thunder!

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:24.120
I knew it!

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:27.660
Thunder was stockpiling energy
from the Power Plant,

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.150
so the energy was coming and going,
like breaths of air!

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.450
Ah! So that’s what it was!

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.230
All right! Then...

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:37.130
Let’s battle, Thunder!

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.810
Let’s go, Pikachu!

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.600
Us, too! Come on, Rabbifoot!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.230
And us!

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:47.940
Yeah!

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.610
Vending, come on!

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.240
All right! All right!

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.320
Rocket...

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.810
Vending...

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:02.200
Secret!

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.760
I wonder, what’ll I get?

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.960
The Drill Pokémon, Saidon!

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.210
All right!
Got a real tough-looking one!

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:19.340
The Trap Pokémon... Maggyo?

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:23.100
Well.
Got a real useless-looking one.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.770
Rabbifoot!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:28.520
Pikachu!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.270
Now it’s gonna attack <i>us,</i> meow!

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:37.420
Oh, dear! A direct hit?!

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.280
It’s over just as quickly
as it began?

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.110
It’s fine, meow!

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:46.790
Both Saidon and Maggyo are part Ground type,
so they’re immune to Electric moves, meow!

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:50.900
Which makes them the perfect pair
to battle Thunder, right?

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:51.880
Yeah!

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.290
Can you believe it?!

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:02.470
We might actually <i>win</i> against
a Legendary Pokémon, meow!

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.190
Go, Saidon! Horn Drill!

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.640
Maggyo! Water Gun!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.080
H-Huh?

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:20.860
What are you doing?!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.670
You’re going completely
the wrong way!

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:25.490
Use Horn Drill on Thunder,
understa—

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:26.910
That was close!

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.750
Well, this is hopeless.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.750
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:36.590
Pikachu!

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.970
We’ll use Lightning Speed, too,
Rabbifoot!

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.980
Rabbifoot! Are you okay?!

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.940
It’s gonna use Thunder again, meow!

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.140
I wanna battle it some more!

00:11:58.140 --> 00:11:59.690
I wanna catch it!

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.570
This is a golden opportunity,
and yet...

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.780
Is there nothing we can do?

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:14.420
What are you gonna do, meow?

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.170
I guess for now...

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.050
...we have no choice but to...

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:24.300
...join forces!

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.380
Raid Battle time!

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:27.180
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.650
Rabbifoot!
Lightning Speed!

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.480
Saidon! Follow along!

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.360
Pikachu! Ride on Maggyo!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.710
Thanks!

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:52.750
That really helped!

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.570
Don’t waste time talking! Attack!

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:57.090
Of course!

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:58.920
Saidon! Rock Blast!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.770
Use Double Kick, Rabbifoot!

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.630
Now! 100,000 Volts!

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.810
Hey! Hold it!

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:15.810
You’re not getting away!

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.030
It’s on the roof.
Let’s chase it!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:26.530
Whoa, there!

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:29.550
We’re done playing nice.

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:31.540
We have but a single goal.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.280
To catch Pikachu, meow!

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:37.180
You keep moving, Go!

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:37.680
But...!

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:39.040
It’s fine! Just hurry!

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.580
Chase down Thunder!

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:43.130
All right!

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:45.440
Give it your all!

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.480
Byenyara!

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:56.260
Of course!

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:57.520
Flygon, go!

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.860
Now! Dragon Claw!

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.870
Flygon!

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:27.720
So sorry we use Pokémon
that are immune to Electric moves!

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:32.220
You see? Pikachu’s
out of electricity, too!

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.890
We might actually win, meow!

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:37.500
As if I’d lose!

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:41.300
Are you okay?

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:43.650
Well, then...

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.360
Dragon Breath!

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:51.740
Yeah!

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.120
Go!

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.370
No good, huh?

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:20.090
How should I fight it?

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:25.220
What an awful feeling!

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:30.220
Go!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.570
Satoshi!

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:40.620
Keep going.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:46.260
Your battle isn’t over yet,
right, Go?

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.840
Of course not!

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:58.060
Flygon! Carry Rabbifoot and fly!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.820
Flygon! Get as close
to Thunder as you can!

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:16.250
All right! Now, Rabbifoot,
use Double Kick!

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:19.950
No good!
It doesn’t have enough reach!

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:27.710
Rabbifoot!

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:50.930
You just wait right there, Thunder!

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:56.710
We’re coming for you!

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.680
Hey, you still not ready? C’mon, hurry up!

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:01.380
Now Flygon, use Draco Meteor!
Hey, you still not ready? C’mon, hurry up!

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.710
You all packed and ready to leave?
Now Flygon, use Draco Meteor!

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:06.660
I’ll show you this wide mysterious world

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.040
And skip the slow send-off

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.940
Be it through fire or through water

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:14.340
I’m fumbling blindly through the days

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.160
When I don’t even know what the next second will bring

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.340
Rabbifoot?!
When I don’t even know what the next second will bring

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.850
When I don’t even know what the next second will bring

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:22.350
Each and every one of my memories

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:23.450
Awesome!
Each and every one of my memories

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.100
Get it, Rabbifoot!
Each and every one of my memories

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:25.880
<i>Now</i> use Double Kick!

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.150
Can always be found inside a Ball
<i>Now</i> use Double Kick!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:30.270
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.840
1: Once the battle’s done

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.820
2: And we’re laughing or crying

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.030
On 3, let’s be friends!

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.600
That wasn’t Double Kick!
On 3, let’s be friends!

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:40.910
It’s Blaze Kick!
On 3, let’s be friends!

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:46.650
Any day and every day, that’s always been my rule

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:48.500
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.940
Rabbifoot!
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:52.130
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:54.610
Let’s go! Every time you trip and fall

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:56.180
Let’s go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:57.650
Please, work...
Let’s go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:58.680
Monster Ball, go!
Let’s go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.760
I choose you!
Monster Ball, go!

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:09.940
Could it be...?

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.320
You got Thunder?!

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:26.480
It didn’t work?

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:31.340
Thunder is summoning
thunderclouds!

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:35.960
Oh, no!

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:41.890
Pikachu!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.640
Are you okay, Pikachu?!

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:57.700
Pikachu got all energetic...

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:00.280
Satoshi!

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.780
Look at that!

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.930
What’s this?

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:07.620
Electric-type Pokémon are gathering.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:19.990
I see! Thunder’s sharing
the lightning with everyone!

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:23.490
“How are you all doing?
Because I’m doing great!”

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.110
Something like that.

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:27.420
Oh... Right. I get it?

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.760
You really don’t, do you?

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.860
I don’t...

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:33.730
But I kinda feel like I do, anyway!

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.280
It’s leaving!

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.830
But I want to catch it!

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:44.510
Guess I gotta give up for today.

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:46.370
But...

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:50.270
The battle with Thunder
was so much fun!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:52.370
I know, right?

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:59.360
See ya, Thunder!

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:01.950
Let’s battle again!

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:26.530
Have a look at this data.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.290
There was a storm growing over the sea
to the southwest, early this morning.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:35.390
It was logged as colliding with
a mysterious biological energy and then vanishing.

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:38.420
You think that “biological energy”
was Thunder?

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.560
Most likely.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:42.920
It probably went to the Power Plant to rest,
being weakened from the storm,

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.840
and received electricity there.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:51.310
So the thunderclouds appearing near Kuchiba City
were caused by Thunder showing up.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.680
Um... Right.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:55.940
Thunder may be found
inside thunderclouds,

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.690
but it can also create them itself!

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:06.220
And Thunder doesn’t just control lightning,
but can gain strength from it as well.

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.060
Yeah!

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:10.390
I got some valuable data
thanks to you two!

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:11.200
Thank you!

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:16.010
Go, this is kinda complex, but...

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:17.460
W-What?

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:21.770
Does the bath come first,
or the super delicious evening meal?

00:21:21.770 --> 00:21:23.240
What do you think?

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:26.020
Well...

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:30.220
Of course the delicious meal
comes first!

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.230
I know, right?!

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:38.310
Though they couldn’t get
the Legendary Pokémon, Thunder,

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:43.080
Satoshi and Go <i>did</i> get an
exciting new discovery!

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:51.530
Pikachu!

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:52.400
Utsubot!

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:53.110
Transel!

00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:53.910
Lugia!

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:54.700
Achamo!

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:55.490
Morpeko!

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:56.200
Koduck!

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:57.080
Cleffy!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:57.780
Eevee!

00:21:57.780 --> 00:21:58.530
Ishitsubute!

00:21:58.530 --> 00:21:59.200
Teppouo!

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:00.120
Onisuzume!

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:00.830
Metagross!

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:01.870
Subame!

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:02.540
Me...

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:03.790
Metamon!

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:20.560
Pikachu!

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:21.390
Usohachi!

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:22.100
Chicorita!

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:22.890
Tamatama!

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:23.640
Mamepato!

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:24.480
Togedemaru!

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.230
Lucario!

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:26.020
Odoshishi!

00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:26.810
Seadra!

00:22:26.810 --> 00:22:27.440
Laplace!

00:22:27.440 --> 00:22:28.270
Starmie!

00:22:28.270 --> 00:22:29.070
Miniryu!

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:29.860
Windie!

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:30.570
Iwark!

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:31.400
Kucheat!

00:22:31.400 --> 00:22:32.150
Togekiss!

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:32.900
Sleep!

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:33.650
Ptera!

00:22:33.650 --> 00:22:34.490
Raikou!

00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:35.240
U’u!

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:36.030
Wooloo!

00:22:36.030 --> 00:22:36.820
Ruriri!

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:37.570
Leafia!

00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:38.370
Armorgaw!

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:39.160
Abagoura!

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:39.950
